@module agents/react
@lang python
@version 0.1.0
@stability experimental
@purpose ReAct agent: an LLM reasons, calls tools, observes results, and loops until it answers
@engine langgraph
@depends [langgraph, langchain_core, langchain_anthropic]
@source https://github.com/example/react-agent
@checkpointer postgres — LangGraph PostgresSaver; conversation state keyed by thread_id
@test_framework pytest
@test_cmd pytest tests/test_agent.py
@aid_version 0.3

---

@type AgentState
@kind struct
@channels
@purpose Shared state threaded through every node of the agent_loop graph
@fields
  messages: [Message] — full conversation incl. tool calls and results. reducer: append.
  step_count: int — number of reason→act cycles taken. reducer: add. Default 0.
  next: str — routing decision written by the planner node. reducer: last-wins.
@invariants
  - messages always starts with a system message and a human message
  - step_count is monotonically non-decreasing
@constructors None — created by the runtime when the graph is invoked with an initial input

---

@type Message
@kind struct
@purpose A single conversation turn (human, AI, or tool result)
@fields
  role: str — One of: system, human, ai, tool.
  content: str — Text content, possibly empty when only tool_calls are present.
  tool_calls: [ToolCall]? — Present on ai messages that request tool invocation.
@implements [Serializable]

---

@type ToolCall
@kind struct
@purpose A model's request to invoke a named tool with arguments
@fields
  id: str — Unique call id, echoed back on the tool result.
  name: str — Tool name. Must match a declared @tool.
  args: dict[str, any] — Arguments validated against the tool's @schema.

---

@type AgentDecision
@kind enum
@purpose Structured output the planner emits to drive routing
@variants
  | Act { tool_calls: [ToolCall] } — at least one tool must run before answering
  | Answer { content: str } — final response, terminate the loop
@implements [Serializable]

---

@model planner_llm
@purpose LLM that reasons about the next step and emits an AgentDecision
@provider anthropic
@model_id claude-opus-4-8
@params temperature=0.0, max_tokens=4096
@structured_output AgentDecision
@determinism nondeterministic
@cost input≈$3/Mtok, output≈$15/Mtok
@effects [Llm, Net]

---

@tool web_search
@purpose Search the web and return ranked results. Use for current events or unknown facts.
@sig (query: str, k?: int) -> [SearchResult] ! SearchError
@params
  query: Search query. Required. Length [1, 400].
  k: Number of results. Default 5. Range [1, 20].
@returns Ranked results, each with title, url, and snippet
@errors
  SearchError.RateLimited — provider quota exceeded [origin]
  SearchError.Network — upstream request failed [origin]
@schema tools/web_search.schema.json
@invoked_by llm
@effects [Net, Tool]
@determinism nondeterministic — results vary with index state
@idempotent true

---

@tool execute_sql
@purpose Run a read-only SQL query against the analytics warehouse
@sig (query: str) -> [Row] ! SqlError
@params
  query: A SELECT statement. Required. Must match ^\s*SELECT.
@returns Result rows as dicts
@errors
  SqlError.Syntax — query failed to parse [origin]
  SqlError.Forbidden — non-SELECT statement rejected [origin]
@schema tools/execute_sql.schema.json
@invoked_by llm
@effects [Db, Tool]
@determinism deterministic
@idempotent true

---

@fn planner_node
@purpose Call the planner LLM and record its decision in state
@sig (state: AgentState) -> AgentState
@params
  state: Current agent state. Required.
@returns State with the AI message appended and `next` set to "act" or "answer"
@effects [Llm, Net]
@reads [AgentState.messages]
@writes [AgentState.messages, AgentState.next, AgentState.step_count]
@calls planner_llm
@determinism nondeterministic

---

@fn tool_executor
@purpose Execute every tool call in the last AI message and append results
@sig (state: AgentState) -> AgentState
@params
  state: Agent state whose last message contains tool_calls. Required.
@returns State with one tool Message appended per executed call
@errors
  SearchError — propagated from web_search [from: web_search]
  SqlError — propagated from execute_sql [from: execute_sql]
@effects [Tool, Net, Db]
@reads [AgentState.messages]
@writes [AgentState.messages]
@calls web_search, execute_sql

---

@fn should_continue
@purpose Router: decide whether to run tools or finish, based on the planner's decision
@sig (state: AgentState) -> str
@params
  state: Agent state with `next` set by planner_node. Required.
@returns "act" if the decision was Act, "END" if it was Answer
@effects None
@reads [AgentState.next]
@determinism deterministic

---

@graph agent_loop
@purpose ReAct loop: reason, act with tools, observe, repeat until the model answers
@engine langgraph
@state AgentState
@entry plan
@nodes
  plan: planner_node — LLM selects the next action [Llm]
  act: tool_executor — runs every requested tool call [Tool]
@edges
  act -> plan
@conditional_edges
  plan: should_continue -> act | END — act if the decision is Act, else END
@cycles
  plan -> act -> plan — bounded by recursion_limit=25; raises GraphRecursionError if exceeded
@interrupts
  before act — human approval required when a tool call targets execute_sql on production
@effects [Llm, Tool, Net, Db]
@antipatterns
  - Don't have tool_executor return the full messages list — the reducer is `append`, so it duplicates history.
  - Don't omit the should_continue exit edge to END — without it the loop only stops at recursion_limit.
@example
  graph = StateGraph(AgentState)
  graph.add_node("plan", planner_node)
  graph.add_node("act", tool_executor)
  graph.set_entry_point("plan")
  graph.add_conditional_edges("plan", should_continue, {"act": "act", "END": END})
  graph.add_edge("act", "plan")
  app = graph.compile(checkpointer=PostgresSaver(...), interrupt_before=["act"])
  result = app.invoke({"messages": [sys, human]}, config={"configurable": {"thread_id": "t1"}})

---

@agent react_agent
@purpose Answers questions by reasoning and calling search/SQL tools in a loop
@model planner_llm
@system_prompt prompts/react_system.md
@tools [web_search, execute_sql]
@autonomy supervised
@guardrails
  - Never run a SQL statement that is not a SELECT [src: agents/react.py:88-96]
  - Stop and answer once enough evidence is gathered; do not loop past recursion_limit
@memory thread
@output str
@effects [Llm, Tool, Net, Db]

---

@invariants
  - The graph must always terminate via the END edge or the recursion_limit; there is no other exit.
    [src: agents/react.py:120-145]
  - Every tool result Message carries the tool_call id it answers, so the model can correlate. [src: agents/react.py:160-172]

---

@workflow run_agent_with_resume
@purpose Invoke the agent, pause for human approval, then resume
@steps
  1. Invoke: app.invoke(input, thread_id) — runs until the `before act` interrupt
  2. Inspect: read the pending tool_calls from the checkpoint
  3. Approve: human confirms or edits the tool call
  4. Resume: app.invoke(None, thread_id) — continues from the interrupt to completion
@errors_at
  step 1: GraphRecursionError — loop exceeded recursion_limit without answering
  step 4: SqlError | SearchError — a tool failed during execution
@antipatterns
  - Don't start a fresh thread_id on resume — the checkpoint is keyed by thread_id; a new id loses all state.
@example
  app.invoke({"messages": [sys, human]}, config={"configurable": {"thread_id": "t1"}})
  # ... interrupt fires; human approves ...
  final = app.invoke(None, config={"configurable": {"thread_id": "t1"}})
